<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Marley returns nine days after his first visit. The clinic&apos;s dermatologist examined the nail with dermoscopy two days after that visit, found a band with irregular lines of varying color and spacing and pigment on the nail fold, and took a full-thickness excisional biopsy of the nail matrix under a digital block. The biopsy shows acral lentiginous melanoma, 0.8 mm thick, not ulcerated. The biopsy site has healed under the dressing; he has needed no pain medicine. He has no lumps in the groin or behind the knee, no cough, headache, or weight loss. Dr. Mbeki-Rowe of surgical oncology saw him this morning and went through the choices for surgery with him at length. He said that his faith, his music and his football all matter to him in this decision, and that he would like to keep the toe if that can be done without lowering his chance of cure. He has had no thoughts of self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Diagnosis</td><td>Acral lentiginous melanoma of the right great toe nail unit, Breslow 0.8 mm, not ulcerated, mitotic rate 1 per mm2</td></tr><tr><td>Clinical stage</td><td>IB (cT1b N0 M0); no symptoms of spread</td></tr><tr><td>Biopsy site</td><td>Healing; no pain medicine needed</td></tr><tr><td>Coordination</td><td>Surgical oncology seen this morning; surgery planned in two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>What matters to him</td><td>His faith, his music and his football; keeping the toe if that is safe</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

